# Code owners for the files that decide whether a change passes: CI workflows, locked tools and their
# suppression/triage/policy files, the scripts that apply them, the review configuration and policies,
# and the install and code-scanning helpers. The last matching pattern wins; every entry names the same
# owner today.
#
# Review by a code owner is NOT required on main (F09 in docs/security-remediation-2026-09-18.md): the
# repository has a single maintainer and enforce_admins is on, so requiring an approval would block every
# merge. GitHub still requests the owner's review on pull requests from anyone else. When a second
# maintainer joins, add them here and turn on "Require review from Code Owners" together with the
# approval, stale-dismissal and last-push settings F09 lists. tests/test_codeowners.py keeps these paths
# covered.

